Z||000004||Blacktree||12-24-2001||02:08 AM||||I remember seeing that one on <A HREF="http://www.beaterz.com" TARGET=_blank>www.beaterz.com</A>  a while back. If I remember correctly, that's the exhaust for the Pratt & Whitney J100 jet engine he's got installed in the trunk.<P>Just kidding   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>Taken from the <A HREF="http://www.beaterz.com" TARGET=_blank>www.beaterz.com</A>  "reviews" section:<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Look! It's a female civic!<P>But seriously folks - what the hell is that thing? A monorail? A new theory on exhaust tip diameter = horsepower? With a pipe like that you need warning stickers to keep the small children away - imagine the liability! Immigration is currently looking into this.... <P>The civics of this era had tail lamps running the full width of the vehicle. The license plate was moved up onto the reflector to make room for that massive protruberance. It's a masterful job - marvel at the genuine soot covering the pipe! Just be sure not to back up in the rain.<P>The exhaust pipe also makes for a handy way to store your civic - just stand it up on end over the nearest fire hydrant. And let's not forget about tailgate parties - it's got a built in grill!<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tweaktech.com" TARGET=_blank>Tweaktech</A><p>[This message has been edited by Blacktree (edited 12-24-2001).]||||reg||1
